WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
MkvDrama.net

3
00:32.762 --> 00:38.120
A wave of simultaneous kidnappings has struck seven cities in Asia!

4
00:40.165 --> 00:42.344
The incidents happened in Tokyo,

5
00:42.498 --> 00:45.105
Seoul, Singapore, Bangkok,

6
00:45.172 --> 00:47.630
Manila, Taipei, and Naha.

7
00:47.714 --> 00:49.339
Seven cities in total.

8
00:50.380 --> 00:55.839
Red rose petals were found at the scene of each crime.

9
00:56.422 --> 01:00.214
Breaking news! Abductions in seven Asian cities!

10
01:40.922 --> 01:42.964
KIDNAP GAME

11
01:45.297 --> 01:49.089
36 HOURS UNTIL THE START OF KIDNAP GAME

12
01:55.282 --> 01:59.059
TOKYO

13
02:03.672 --> 02:06.922
AM 07:02 JST

14
02:12.755 --> 02:16.005
DETECTIVE TOSHIRO NIIDE

15
02:25.960 --> 02:27.135
Saori!

16
02:33.188 --> 02:35.772
You're crushing me.

17
02:38.897 --> 02:40.272
Oh...

18
02:42.563 --> 02:44.730
Thanks for waking me.

19
02:46.188 --> 02:48.556
-What's that? -I bought it for tomorrow.

20
02:50.105 --> 02:52.776
Tomorrow? The Tokyo Festival?

21
02:53.063 --> 02:54.756
No.

22
02:55.647 --> 02:56.576
Did you forget?

23
02:58.980 --> 03:04.236
No way I'd forget. It's our... tenth.

24
03:04.688 --> 03:07.772
Our gold anniversary. Wait, silver?

25
03:07.843 --> 03:11.130
Uh-huh. Your coffee's getting cold.

26
03:15.233 --> 03:16.690
Thanks for protecting me.

27
03:24.188 --> 03:26.522
It's bigger than ever this year.

28
03:26.688 --> 03:31.647
The festivities include a parade and a greeting from foreign guests.

29
03:31.931 --> 03:33.780
A large turnout is expected.

30
03:34.253 --> 03:38.560
Traffic restrictions will be placed around the venue.

31
03:39.064 --> 03:43.352
The police will dispatch units to direct traffic and enhance security.

32
03:45.855 --> 03:47.813
I wonder if we'll see the fireworks.

33
03:48.147 --> 03:51.022
The new, big condo might block the view.

34
03:51.850 --> 03:55.392
No. I mean can we see them together?

35
03:57.522 --> 03:58.397
Sure we can.

36
03:58.778 --> 04:00.486
Aren't you on duty?

37
04:00.563 --> 04:01.688
I am.

38
04:01.772 --> 04:04.813
But I get off after the parade at five.

39
04:10.000 --> 04:13.458
It starts at seven, so you'll make it.

40
04:13.515 --> 04:15.182
Yeah. Delicious, thanks.

41
04:17.685 --> 04:18.851
What about you?

42
04:19.235 --> 04:23.522
I think I can get off early, so I'll cook us a nice dinner.

43
04:23.926 --> 04:28.343
A nice dinner, huh? Then could you grab some champagne?

44
04:28.905 --> 04:33.488
Don't you mean beer? Hey, I found a delicious craft beer.

45
04:34.145 --> 04:35.645
Looking forward to it.

46
04:39.027 --> 04:40.319
That was delicious.

47
04:49.333 --> 04:51.875
-Well, I'll be off. -Have a good day.

48
04:54.125 --> 04:58.708
Grandma? Michiyo?

49
04:59.625 --> 05:02.666
Mr. Tadokoro, is your wife missing?

50
05:02.750 --> 05:06.083
Yeah, she's probably lost again.

51
05:06.166 --> 05:08.125
Did anything unusual happen?

52
05:09.886 --> 05:12.678
Ah... the bread for breakfast.

53
05:13.337 --> 05:14.212
Bread?

54
05:16.706 --> 05:19.915
She said something about forgetting to buy it.

55
05:22.625 --> 05:26.125
Mrs. Tadokoro! Good morning. It's me, Niide.

56
05:26.516 --> 05:30.058
Your husband's looking for you. Let's go home.

57
05:30.474 --> 05:31.891
Okay? Let's go.

58
05:31.975 --> 05:33.250
That's one thousand yen.

59
05:34.094 --> 05:36.761
Huh? Ah...

60
05:36.931 --> 05:42.848
You don't have your wallet... I guess not.

61
05:48.208 --> 05:49.750
Mind the steps.

62
05:53.458 --> 05:54.791
Okay, let's go.

63
05:57.041 --> 06:00.213
-You got bread. -This bakery is delicious!

64
06:00.291 --> 06:01.333
Is that so?

65
06:01.375 --> 06:04.500
FLOWER SHOP ATRA

66
06:07.458 --> 06:11.666
SEOUL

67
06:14.625 --> 06:18.166
AM 08:08 KST

68
06:29.291 --> 06:32.750
DOCTOR HAN KIJU

69
06:35.708 --> 06:42.791
HANDS OF GOD DOCTOR ENJOYS EASY RETIREMENT

70
06:45.166 --> 06:49.625
WIFE IS COSMETICS MOGUL BLIND DAUGHTER IS VIOLIN PRODIGY

71
06:52.708 --> 06:57.333
ALL BECAUSE OF HIS DAUGHTER'S FAILED SURGERY?!

72
07:07.958 --> 07:09.375
Rian?

73
07:11.875 --> 07:14.041
Let's get ready for school.

74
07:14.345 --> 07:15.679
I'll take that.

75
07:22.755 --> 07:23.797
Rian.

76
07:24.088 --> 07:25.879
It was great. Thanks.

77
07:27.039 --> 07:28.122
Sure.

78
07:30.198 --> 07:31.070
Up you go.

79
07:41.009 --> 07:42.343
Have you read this?

80
07:42.901 --> 07:44.526
Such a load of garbage.

81
07:45.530 --> 07:47.000
Don't let it bother you.

82
07:47.271 --> 07:49.640
They're even sensationalizing Rian.

83
07:55.541 --> 08:02.541
Rian, about your recital tomorrow... Mom might not make it.

84
08:04.375 --> 08:09.458
It can't be helped if Mom is busy. What about you, Dad?

85
08:09.583 --> 08:13.125
Me? I'll go for sure.

86
08:14.217 --> 08:16.424
You won't have an urgent surgery?

87
08:17.960 --> 08:19.252
Don't worry.

88
08:19.338 --> 08:22.588
There are plenty of other good doctors.

89
08:23.557 --> 08:27.849
I see. But don't mind me if they need you, okay?

90
08:29.003 --> 08:33.128
Your job is to save people's lives, after all.

91
08:36.916 --> 08:39.958
Yes, that's right.

92
08:52.250 --> 08:54.291
FLOWER SHOP ATRA

93
08:57.250 --> 09:00.750
SINGAPORE

94
09:08.875 --> 09:11.958
FLIGHT ATTENDANT JANICE LAU

95
09:13.166 --> 09:17.125
Sorry, I'm late. Got stuck in traffic.

96
09:21.284 --> 09:22.367
Janice!

97
09:25.618 --> 09:26.216
Sorry.

98
09:27.829 --> 09:29.204
He proposed?!

99
09:29.329 --> 09:31.121
Not yet.

100
09:31.204 --> 09:33.371
But he did booked Monti Marina Bay tomorrow.

101
09:33.496 --> 09:36.788
No way! You’ve almost got your meal ticket!

102
09:36.913 --> 09:39.954
What are you talking about? The meal ticket’s just a bonus.

103
09:40.496 --> 09:42.871
Tony’s a really sweet guy.

104
09:43.805 --> 09:46.513
What do you think I should wear tomorrow?

105
09:47.256 --> 09:50.214
You know, I don’t want to overdo it, y’know...

106
09:50.246 --> 09:54.996
It’s not about clothes. It’s about showing up on time.

107
09:55.913 --> 09:59.496
Don’t worry, I’ll be on time even if it kills me.

108
10:04.788 --> 10:06.454
FLOWER SHOP ATRA

109
10:09.288 --> 10:12.913
BANGKOK

110
10:14.163 --> 10:16.704
AM 08:46 ICT

111
10:17.098 --> 10:18.140
Aum.

112
10:18.288 --> 10:19.329
HOSTESS AUM THANAWAN

113
10:19.454 --> 10:21.413
You're still smoking this?

114
10:21.663 --> 10:23.512
I thought you already quit!

115
10:27.292 --> 10:29.000
I don't use it anymore.

116
10:29.579 --> 10:31.621
Then what's this?

117
10:34.746 --> 10:39.688
Are you still dealing? Why, Aum?!

118
10:41.079 --> 10:43.247
It's the only way I know how to live!

119
10:53.371 --> 10:54.746
FLOWER SHOP ATRA

120
10:57.579 --> 11:01.038
MANILA

121
11:03.216 --> 11:06.799
PM 02:07 PHT

122
11:08.079 --> 11:09.871
TAXI DRIVER MIGUEL GARCIA

123
11:09.967 --> 11:14.416
Are you from Japan?

124
11:15.129 --> 11:17.768
Yeah, we're on our honeymoon.

125
11:18.499 --> 11:22.915
-Hey, your Japanese is great! -Thanks.

126
11:23.173 --> 11:27.673
I used to work in Tokyo.

127
11:28.371 --> 11:33.514
Have you been to the Manila Baywalk Dolomite beach?

128
11:35.031 --> 11:39.364
They say if you see that emerald sea at...

129
11:41.246 --> 11:47.538
3 p.m, if you see the sea, your love will last forever.

130
11:48.406 --> 11:50.656
It doesn’t say that in the guidebook.

131
11:51.469 --> 11:55.844
It’s veery famous among the youth in Manila.

132
11:56.224 --> 12:00.258
My 20-year-old granddaughter told me.

133
12:01.704 --> 12:03.131
-Wow! -Wow!

134
12:03.306 --> 12:06.305
-It's so beautiful. -It really is.

135
12:25.788 --> 12:27.996
FLOWER SHOP ATRA

136
12:30.871 --> 12:34.454
TAIPEI

137
12:38.913 --> 12:42.121
AM 10:48 TST

138
13:02.704 --> 13:06.538
HOUSEWIFE CHRISTINA LIN

139
13:09.450 --> 13:10.742
What's wrong?

140
13:13.154 --> 13:14.579
You're not filming again are you?

141
13:15.564 --> 13:17.806
No! And I deleted the old video.

142
13:21.855 --> 13:23.314
Don't you believe me?

143
13:30.189 --> 13:31.189
Christina...

144
13:32.814 --> 13:33.685
You're my one true love.

145
13:34.980 --> 13:36.219
I want to be with you.

146
13:37.272 --> 13:38.385
Don't you trust me?

147
13:41.314 --> 13:42.091
I do.

148
13:53.980 --> 13:55.772
ATRA FLOWER SHOP

149
13:58.605 --> 14:02.355
NAHA

150
14:06.064 --> 14:09.730
PM 12:49 JST

151
14:13.105 --> 14:15.980
SYSTEMS ENGINEER KURANOSUKE HIGA

152
14:16.105 --> 14:19.397
It's ready. I made your favorite.

153
14:21.980 --> 14:24.022
I told you that we'll eat out.

154
14:24.522 --> 14:26.355
What for?

155
14:29.980 --> 14:34.814
Would it be okay if I invite some old friends over?

156
14:34.939 --> 14:37.439
Like former co-workers and neighbors.

157
14:37.522 --> 14:41.564
You think they'll like that? They'll only resent you.

158
14:42.272 --> 14:43.314
I miss them.

159
14:43.397 --> 14:46.397
You're here now! In my world!

160
14:46.897 --> 14:50.314
Don't you get it? Your son is a world-famous CEO!

161
15:15.230 --> 15:17.564
FLOWER SHOP ATRA

162
15:19.939 --> 15:22.564
30 HOURS UNTIL THE START OF KIDNAP GAME

163
15:28.314 --> 15:29.939
This is the police.

164
15:41.814 --> 15:42.856
Shut up.

165
15:43.802 --> 15:48.510
I'm Niide. Community Safety Division, Shinjuku Central.

166
15:48.739 --> 15:51.864
We got a call about a child screaming.

167
15:52.105 --> 15:52.855
Get lost.

168
15:52.914 --> 15:53.872
Hey...

169
15:57.432 --> 16:00.640
What a jerk. That's a wife-beater for sure.

170
16:11.230 --> 16:14.522
-Stop it! -You shut your mouth!

171
16:14.647 --> 16:18.855
-Stop it! -Shut up! Get away from me!

172
16:21.230 --> 16:23.924
My life's a mess because of you!

173
16:24.033 --> 16:26.158
Stop it, Dad!

174
16:26.911 --> 16:30.078
Get off, you little shit!

175
16:30.296 --> 16:32.671
-You piece of shit! -You okay?

176
16:34.630 --> 16:36.344
Stop it!

177
17:00.257 --> 17:01.632
What's the matter?

178
17:02.286 --> 17:04.749
We can't just leave.

179
17:12.955 --> 17:16.876
Next, we make an incision in the dura along the nerve

180
17:17.300 --> 17:21.550
to expose C3 and give us a wider surgical field.

181
17:22.700 --> 17:26.620
This allows us to temporarily clamp the blood vessel,

182
17:26.779 --> 17:31.529
making it safer to perform aneurysm clipping and tumor resection.

183
17:35.407 --> 17:37.396
Dr. Han, thank you for the lecture.

184
17:37.979 --> 17:38.716
Please.

185
17:40.997 --> 17:47.039
Have you thought about it? I'd like you to take on that surgery.

186
17:47.290 --> 17:51.248
Like I said before, I have another lecture scheduled.

187
17:51.406 --> 17:56.198
The patient's a big-shot politician with pull in the art world.

188
17:56.357 --> 17:57.982
Think of your daughter.

189
17:58.014 --> 17:59.639
I'm sorry.

190
18:02.172 --> 18:03.099
Now if you'll excuse me.

191
18:26.321 --> 18:28.169
Will she lose her sight?

192
18:29.376 --> 18:31.335
You said it would succeed.

193
18:32.689 --> 18:35.105
You said you'd fix her eyes.

194
18:50.164 --> 18:51.110
Excuse me, Dr. Han?

195
18:53.860 --> 18:57.243
I'm Park Dongkuk, Midum Funeral Services.

196
19:01.668 --> 19:04.752
Good luck to your daughter for her recital.

197
19:07.471 --> 19:08.805
Don't look baffled.

198
19:09.335 --> 19:12.085
I know everything about you, Doctor.

199
19:12.216 --> 19:15.174
So if you ever need help, let me know.

200
19:24.185 --> 19:27.602
That probably won't be necessary.

201
19:48.059 --> 19:50.716
We can't do anything without a warrant.

202
20:12.915 --> 20:14.540
Police! Open up!

203
20:15.393 --> 20:16.768
Open up!

204
20:17.368 --> 20:18.808
I told you to get lost.

205
20:18.973 --> 20:20.098
Niide!

206
20:20.593 --> 20:21.759
Hey!

207
20:29.147 --> 20:31.064
Hyodo! Hold him down!

208
20:32.744 --> 20:35.827
Get your filthy hands off!

209
20:47.895 --> 20:51.395
Put your anger aside. Show your kindness...

210
20:52.425 --> 20:57.091
Kindness that shields the weak...

211
20:57.453 --> 21:02.703
That's the right thing to do.

212
21:06.580 --> 21:08.330
-Hyodo. -Yes.

213
21:13.605 --> 21:17.598
Come on out. You okay? C'mon.

214
21:20.829 --> 21:21.850
It's okay now.

215
21:23.629 --> 21:26.856
You protected your mom.

216
21:30.944 --> 21:32.083
You did well.

217
21:36.367 --> 21:38.023
You're not pregnant.

218
21:40.271 --> 21:41.403
I see.

219
21:44.160 --> 21:45.577
My mistake.

220
21:45.859 --> 21:49.210
Might be good to get your husband tested.

221
21:52.708 --> 21:53.343
Okay.

222
22:05.601 --> 22:08.185
SAORI NEW MESSAGE

223
22:08.310 --> 22:10.351
24 HOURS UNTIL THE GAME STARTS

224
22:10.680 --> 22:13.775
"Twenty-four hours until the game starts."

225
22:14.376 --> 22:16.283
-Niide! -Coming.

226
22:26.792 --> 22:28.542
My sincerest apologies.

227
22:29.126 --> 22:30.334
For what?

228
22:31.709 --> 22:35.167
For this...

229
22:35.792 --> 22:39.265
How many times do I have to tell you?

230
22:39.290 --> 22:40.725
I didn't hit him.

231
22:40.751 --> 22:45.001
Damn right you didn't! You think we're in the seventies?!

232
22:45.251 --> 22:46.917
But sir, you also...

233
22:47.542 --> 22:50.209
-Huh? -Er, nothing.

234
22:53.626 --> 22:56.584
Well, now you're outta my hair.

235
23:00.159 --> 23:01.076
Transferal?

236
23:01.209 --> 23:03.584
ASSIGNED TO HOMICIDE DIVISION

237
23:08.398 --> 23:09.648
NISHI-SHINJUKU MEDICAL CENTER

238
23:09.834 --> 23:13.726
-Take care. -You too.

239
23:16.751 --> 23:20.220
Might be good to get your husband tested.

240
23:31.242 --> 23:34.242
-Yes? -Sorry, I'll be late tonight.

241
23:35.786 --> 23:40.075
Are you going somewhere? There's something I'd like to talk about.

242
23:40.626 --> 23:43.292
I got transferred to the Homicide Division.

243
23:44.051 --> 23:48.176
The Homicide Division? That's great!

244
23:48.278 --> 23:50.542
-Niide, let's go! -Okay.

245
23:50.626 --> 23:53.458
Saori! We're borrowing Niide!

246
23:54.159 --> 23:55.659
They want to celebrate.

247
23:56.434 --> 23:59.559
Can't do without the guest of honor.

248
24:00.172 --> 24:01.438
Sorry. Bye.

249
24:07.332 --> 24:08.124
Congratulations.

250
24:14.459 --> 24:17.092
Tonight, we're here to celebrate...

251
24:17.126 --> 24:19.667
Cheers!

252
24:20.001 --> 24:21.876
You just had to, huh?

253
24:21.959 --> 24:25.636
Niide, let's drink till we drop!

254
24:25.975 --> 24:27.184
Got it.

255
24:27.242 --> 24:29.284
-Cheers. -Cheers. Thanks.

256
24:31.714 --> 24:35.256
-You drank waaay too much. -I'm not drunk.

257
24:35.686 --> 24:38.352
Stairs ahead. Turning here.

258
24:40.001 --> 24:42.501
-We're boarding. -Wait a sec...

259
24:42.546 --> 24:45.129
-Whoa, whoa. -We're boarding.

260
25:04.959 --> 25:06.209
Oh, sorry.

261
25:19.167 --> 25:20.459
Excuse me...

262
25:21.959 --> 25:23.870
Do you know the trolley problem?

263
25:25.584 --> 25:26.343
Huh?

264
25:27.934 --> 25:29.229
The trolley problem.

265
25:31.284 --> 25:37.796
The one about the uncontrollable trolley on the rails?

266
25:38.664 --> 25:39.664
Yes.

267
25:40.351 --> 25:42.934
If the trolley runs straight,

268
25:43.123 --> 25:47.392
five workers on the track ahead die.

269
25:47.470 --> 25:52.345
If you press a button to divert it to save those five,

270
25:52.417 --> 25:57.501
one different worker on the other track dies.

271
25:58.209 --> 26:02.626
Now, if you were there, would you press that button?

272
26:05.459 --> 26:12.167
I think... I'd try to save the five some other way.

273
26:12.858 --> 26:14.733
Interesting...

274
26:15.648 --> 26:19.523
Then let's change the rules a bit.

275
26:20.127 --> 26:23.607
Say there's one person straight ahead,

276
26:23.874 --> 26:28.082
and five on the other line.

277
26:28.338 --> 26:32.338
And all you can do is press the button, or not.

278
26:34.125 --> 26:39.345
And what if the solo person is...

279
26:41.186 --> 26:42.561
your wife.

280
26:46.644 --> 26:49.394
Would you kill the five?

281
26:56.721 --> 27:01.340
I guess it's hard to answer a question like that out of the blue.

282
27:03.143 --> 27:04.268
Yeah.

283
27:06.098 --> 27:11.931
But there'll come a day when you have to decide.

284
27:30.204 --> 27:32.204
See you around, Detective.

285
27:33.721 --> 27:36.346
"Detective?" Hey, wait...

286
28:44.346 --> 28:47.235
The person I admire the most is my dad.

287
28:47.754 --> 28:49.852
He is a doctor.

288
28:50.387 --> 28:53.663
My dad's job is saving people's lives.

289
28:54.093 --> 28:58.556
I want to become someone who can save people, just like him.

290
29:32.846 --> 29:34.346
I'm home.

291
29:50.861 --> 29:54.254
You weren't always this studious. Did you decide on a goal?

292
29:55.614 --> 29:57.614
Yeah, police officer.

293
29:58.108 --> 30:00.275
Huh, I wouldn't have guessed.

294
30:00.739 --> 30:03.660
Did you decide to do what's right for society?

295
30:07.929 --> 30:11.370
I think Mom had an unhappy life.

296
30:13.503 --> 30:16.921
I'm not so sure. She had you, after all.

297
30:17.429 --> 30:21.637
It was because of me that she couldn't leave that jerk.

298
30:24.066 --> 30:27.123
I couldn't protect her.

299
30:34.637 --> 30:38.762
This is Carrot-Man. He's kind of a... good-luck charm.

300
30:39.096 --> 30:40.762
Feel free to throw him out.

301
30:41.637 --> 30:43.054
Why a carrot?

302
30:43.596 --> 30:47.804
Your short fuse is because you don't eat enough carrots.

303
30:48.290 --> 30:49.207
Irrelevant.

304
30:50.038 --> 30:53.621
Promise Carrot-Man that you won't get angry.

305
30:54.196 --> 30:55.112
No.

306
30:55.368 --> 30:56.660
So you don’t want him?

307
30:56.846 --> 30:59.248
No... I'll keep him.

308
31:02.280 --> 31:03.446
Thanks.

309
31:10.762 --> 31:14.012
Ah, they're starting. Let's go.

310
31:17.971 --> 31:19.387
What?

311
31:32.304 --> 31:35.804
-So pretty. -Awesome.

312
31:40.528 --> 31:41.861
Let's do this again.

313
31:43.412 --> 31:46.037
-Next year? -Yes, next year.

314
31:46.221 --> 31:47.971
And the year after.

315
31:48.183 --> 31:53.933
Yeah. Every year, together.

316
31:57.608 --> 32:00.525
We'll watch them together every year.

317
32:47.554 --> 32:56.471
12 HOURS UNTIL THE START OF KIDNAP GAME

318
32:56.596 --> 33:00.721
TOKYO FESTIVAL 2026

319
33:00.804 --> 33:05.650
Welcome to TOKYO FESTIVAL. Parade starts at 10 AM. Fireworks at 7 PM.

320
33:10.702 --> 33:13.455
What a turnout.

321
33:14.247 --> 33:16.039
Lot of tourists, too.

322
33:16.955 --> 33:20.205
And VIPs from all over the world.

323
33:20.289 --> 33:21.330
VIPs?

324
33:21.414 --> 33:23.788
Mic test, mic test. One, two, three.

325
33:24.120 --> 33:25.247
-How is it? -Okay.

326
33:25.417 --> 33:26.368
Thank you.

327
33:31.816 --> 33:33.066
Excuse me.

328
33:35.772 --> 33:36.794
Hello?

329
33:37.201 --> 33:40.921
Akina? Sorry, I'll call back if you're busy.

330
33:40.992 --> 33:42.784
It's fine. What's up?

331
33:44.419 --> 33:46.336
It's just about Toshiro.

332
33:46.432 --> 33:48.474
What did he do this time?

333
33:49.534 --> 33:53.534
No, he's been transferred to the Homicide Division.

334
33:53.619 --> 33:58.243
Huh? So his dream has come true at last. That's fantastic.

335
33:59.416 --> 34:00.303
Thanks.

336
34:00.735 --> 34:03.902
But he's gonna get even busier, isn't he?

337
34:04.987 --> 34:09.403
You haven't told him about the test yet, right?

338
34:10.713 --> 34:12.497
Well... no.

339
34:12.580 --> 34:17.622
How's holding back gonna help? Think about yourself for a change.

340
34:19.039 --> 34:22.789
Sorry, there's a patient. I'll call you back.

341
34:23.872 --> 34:25.747
Is everything okay?

342
34:26.747 --> 34:28.039
Huh?

343
34:30.048 --> 34:31.673
-He's all yours. -Okay.

344
34:31.830 --> 34:33.455
Take care.

345
34:34.205 --> 34:36.330
Take your time.

346
34:37.839 --> 34:39.889
-Hey there. -Hello.

347
34:39.914 --> 34:42.622
Have you had lunch? I've got one left.

348
34:42.845 --> 34:45.179
-Can I buy that? -Sure can!

349
34:45.686 --> 34:47.477
I'll knock 200 yen off.

350
34:48.016 --> 34:49.014
You're too kind.

351
34:54.904 --> 34:56.279
I LOVE YOU MOMMY

352
34:56.437 --> 34:59.228
Is that by your... daughter?

353
35:01.284 --> 35:06.456
Yup. My pride and joy. Cute as a button, unlike me.

354
35:07.409 --> 35:11.617
She's my reason for living. My whole life, even.

355
35:14.366 --> 35:15.449
I'm jealous.

356
35:16.191 --> 35:18.056
Of course, it's not all easy.

357
35:24.663 --> 35:30.288
That van was also there yesterday. I wonder what it is.

358
35:31.192 --> 35:34.609
A florist, perhaps?

359
35:36.617 --> 35:38.201
Maybe a coincidence.

360
35:41.784 --> 35:44.367
FLOWER SHOP ATRA

361
36:03.018 --> 36:04.579
What's the occasion?

362
36:05.379 --> 36:09.159
I want to give my daughter a bouquet.

363
36:09.826 --> 36:11.326
Come on in.

364
36:16.064 --> 36:18.112
How about something like this?

365
36:22.701 --> 36:27.205
Wow, they're distinctive. Would a kid like these?

366
36:27.663 --> 36:33.163
They have a unique fragrance. I'm sure your daughter will appreciate them.

367
36:35.576 --> 36:36.909
Oh, yes.

368
36:38.367 --> 36:41.034
How do you know she's blind?

369
36:47.451 --> 36:49.409
That's a message from us.

370
36:50.784 --> 36:52.659
THE GAME BEGINS IN 5 HOURS.

371
36:54.451 --> 36:55.909
What's...

372
37:06.703 --> 37:08.870
Welcome. Can I help you?

373
37:10.992 --> 37:14.159
The other shop assistant...

374
37:15.618 --> 37:18.368
I'm the only one working here.

375
37:35.365 --> 37:36.365
Niide.

376
37:37.348 --> 37:39.967
-A VIP will pass Point A shortly. -Okay.

377
37:40.212 --> 37:42.296
-Be on alert. -Yes, sir.

378
37:42.971 --> 37:44.262
Hi, guys.

379
37:44.346 --> 37:46.137
Good to see you.

380
37:46.221 --> 37:48.137
They got you on security?

381
37:48.221 --> 37:51.637
You Community Safety guys don't have it easy.

382
37:52.054 --> 37:55.346
Niide got transferred to the Homicide Division.

383
37:55.429 --> 37:56.804
So I heard.

384
37:56.887 --> 37:59.080
Congrats. Saori was delighted.

385
37:59.929 --> 38:02.554
It's your wedding anniversary, too.

386
38:02.637 --> 38:05.346
Just go back to your post.

387
38:08.799 --> 38:12.049
And? What did you get for her?

388
38:12.262 --> 38:13.721
-Huh? -Huh?

389
38:14.346 --> 38:16.346
You didn't get her anything?

390
38:16.679 --> 38:21.012
Don't you know you only made it this far thanks to her?

391
38:21.387 --> 38:23.387
Of course, I'm grateful.

392
38:26.554 --> 38:28.762
You know what's troubling her?

393
38:29.679 --> 38:30.846
Kinda...

394
38:31.637 --> 38:34.179
I think you need to address that.

395
38:36.054 --> 38:37.137
Yeah.

396
38:44.596 --> 38:48.304
Excuse me. Do you have Hoshikuzu beer?

397
38:48.387 --> 38:51.096
I'm sorry, we don't stock that.

398
38:51.596 --> 38:53.262
I see. Thank you.

399
38:53.887 --> 38:58.221
We're done, but keep an eye out. I'll notify you on pullout.

400
38:58.304 --> 38:59.221
Yes, sir.

401
38:59.471 --> 39:01.346
-Niide. -Yes.

402
39:01.429 --> 39:04.387
Could you see the guests to their car?

403
39:05.054 --> 39:07.637
But I'm off-duty now, sir.

404
39:07.721 --> 39:11.846
Come on... take one for your old team.

405
39:12.762 --> 39:14.637
All right, sir.

406
39:28.096 --> 39:29.929
MUSIC ACHIEVEMENT SHOWCASE

407
39:30.012 --> 39:33.471
DONGHAE ARTS CENTER

408
39:34.179 --> 39:36.429
-This way. -Thank you.

409
39:42.512 --> 39:44.304
Rian, your dad's here.

410
39:51.387 --> 39:52.512
Rian.

411
39:52.929 --> 39:54.221
Dad!

412
39:56.679 --> 39:59.137
You look lovely.

413
40:00.012 --> 40:01.554
This is for you.

414
40:05.804 --> 40:09.679
Thanks. They smell nice.

415
40:17.554 --> 40:25.054
Mom... really wanted to come, but she had too much work.

416
40:25.762 --> 40:26.971
That's a shame, huh

417
40:28.679 --> 40:32.179
It's okay. You made it.

418
40:37.405 --> 40:40.523
You know, I can see it.

419
40:44.029 --> 40:47.975
No matter where, no matter when, I can see your smile, Dad.

420
41:10.159 --> 41:13.243
Thank you.

421
41:28.846 --> 41:33.429
1 HOUR UNTIL THE START OF KIDNAP GAME

422
42:07.554 --> 42:08.721
Niide.

423
42:09.332 --> 42:12.647
I'll write the report. Please, go home.

424
42:12.773 --> 42:14.689
I owe you one. Thanks.

425
42:16.364 --> 42:17.905
Welcome.

426
42:26.935 --> 42:30.227
The language... of flowers...

427
42:33.637 --> 42:35.721
"Together forever."

428
42:38.555 --> 42:41.347
"You are perfect."

429
42:42.558 --> 42:44.558
"Dearest."

430
42:46.564 --> 42:48.105
This is it.

431
42:48.612 --> 42:50.987
Can I get eleven white roses?

432
43:00.012 --> 43:01.429
Found it.

433
43:42.510 --> 43:47.144
Well, you had everyone transfixed today.

434
43:47.356 --> 43:48.898
You were like an angel.

435
43:49.021 --> 43:50.855
-Really? -Yup.

436
43:51.547 --> 43:53.589
I wish Mom could have seen.

437
43:53.923 --> 43:57.596
I'll be sure to bring Mom next time, okay?

438
43:57.912 --> 43:58.995
Okay.

439
44:02.070 --> 44:03.237
Just a sec.

440
44:06.012 --> 44:09.116
EMERGENCY. CALL BACK AT ONCE.

441
44:12.852 --> 44:14.977
Uh, Rian, just a sec.

442
44:19.497 --> 44:21.289
Up we go.

443
44:23.298 --> 44:28.507
I just have to make a quick call to the hospital.

444
44:28.858 --> 44:31.858
-Can you wait for me here? -Okay.

445
45:10.887 --> 45:14.679
This is Han Kiju. I got a message about an emergency.

446
45:15.212 --> 45:18.337
Ah, Dr. Han. I'll check right away.

447
45:18.865 --> 45:20.143
Please do.

448
45:28.311 --> 45:30.227
Sorry to keep you waiting.

449
45:31.745 --> 45:33.079
Oh, it's fine.

450
45:56.198 --> 45:59.198
SORRY, RUNNING A BIT LATE

451
46:00.221 --> 46:05.012
1 MINUTE UNTIL THE START OF KIDNAP GAME

452
46:09.136 --> 46:13.322
I'm telling you, I got a message about an emergency.

453
46:13.467 --> 46:17.842
But nobody here says they sent the message.

454
46:20.179 --> 46:21.596
What on earth...?

455
46:29.713 --> 46:31.338
What pretty flowers.

456
46:34.907 --> 46:36.782
Thank you.

457
46:39.505 --> 46:44.172
Doesn't this smell nice too?

458
46:45.221 --> 46:48.563
30 SECONDS UNTIL THE START OF KIDNAP GAME

459
46:53.270 --> 46:58.353
What color do you think this rose is?

460
47:01.490 --> 47:03.184
Red?

461
47:03.209 --> 47:04.292
No.

462
47:05.815 --> 47:06.848
It's black.

463
47:08.608 --> 47:09.858
It's a black rose.

464
47:19.367 --> 47:22.117
SORRY, RUNNING A BIT LATE

465
47:54.554 --> 47:57.696
And now it's time for the main event.

466
47:58.307 --> 48:00.298
In a few moments,

467
48:00.330 --> 48:05.455
the fireworks bearing our hopes and dreams will light up the sky.

468
48:06.557 --> 48:11.890
Now let's bring the Tokyo night sky to life with the ultimate countdown!

469
48:16.814 --> 48:19.022
Here we go!

470
48:19.185 --> 48:25.435
Ten! Nine! Eight! Seven! Six!

471
48:25.814 --> 48:26.939
Five!

472
48:27.022 --> 48:28.231
Four!

473
48:28.314 --> 48:29.647
Three!

474
48:29.731 --> 48:30.647
Two!

475
48:30.731 --> 48:32.606
One!

476
49:43.522 --> 49:44.689
Rian?

477
49:46.606 --> 49:47.606
Rian!

478
49:49.772 --> 49:50.856
Rian!

479
51:06.272 --> 51:07.439
Saori?

480
51:28.897 --> 51:30.356
Something happen?

481
51:31.522 --> 51:35.147
-She saw a kidnapping. -Tell us what you remember.

482
51:35.272 --> 51:37.314
-I saw... -Mrs. Tadokoro.

483
51:38.064 --> 51:39.397
Your wife!

484
51:39.772 --> 51:43.064
I saw a florist take your wife away!

485
51:43.439 --> 51:46.022
-Huh? -I really saw it!

486
51:50.981 --> 51:52.189
Pause it.

487
51:53.223 --> 51:54.723
That's Saori.

488
51:56.240 --> 51:57.566
Please play it.

489
52:04.505 --> 52:06.547
That's Saori. My wife.

490
52:06.622 --> 52:08.751
Code red! Track down the van.

491
52:08.776 --> 52:09.735
Yes, sir.

492
52:12.856 --> 52:15.981
-You said it was a florist. -My wife did.

493
52:16.661 --> 52:19.286
Yes! This is the van.

494
52:19.363 --> 52:22.363
It turned right at the tee.

495
52:29.356 --> 52:34.788
Rian can't see. She wouldn't go home on her own!

496
52:34.887 --> 52:36.220
Please calm down.

497
52:36.266 --> 52:38.932
How do you expect me to calm down?!

498
52:42.505 --> 52:46.921
It was a woman.

499
52:49.704 --> 52:52.662
She left these rose petals behind.

500
52:56.857 --> 53:01.357
Have any of you seen my daughter?

501
53:01.857 --> 53:03.815
Have none of you seen her?

502
53:04.831 --> 53:10.164
My daughter is about... about this tall...

503
53:10.189 --> 53:12.914
She's wearing a white coat.

504
53:12.939 --> 53:14.814
If anyone has seen her, please tell me!

505
53:18.731 --> 53:22.147
Stand back, stand back. Please make way.

506
53:24.439 --> 53:26.689
-Make way. -Coming through.

507
53:40.269 --> 53:42.781
-Here's a copy of the map. -Thanks.

508
53:42.806 --> 53:45.722
They can't be far. Hyodo, where's the van?

509
53:45.891 --> 53:46.974
Um, I don't...

510
53:47.038 --> 53:49.872
-Use the N System, goddammit! -Calm down!

511
53:50.962 --> 53:53.962
Don't forget, you're a part to this, so...

512
53:53.987 --> 53:55.737
I know that!

513
53:56.372 --> 53:58.539
She's my wife!

514
53:59.553 --> 54:01.012
That's why I...

515
54:01.095 --> 54:02.345
Hold on.

516
54:02.720 --> 54:08.176
You know it's standard procedure to wait for the demands in a missing persons case.

517
54:08.887 --> 54:12.843
The SIT is taking over. There are press controls in place.

518
54:14.095 --> 54:15.630
Your job is to cooperate.

519
54:27.470 --> 54:29.220
AKINA ISOBE

520
54:33.553 --> 54:34.345
Hello?

521
54:34.527 --> 54:36.014
I heard about Saori.

522
54:36.690 --> 54:37.856
I can't talk.

523
54:37.881 --> 54:41.006
Listen! Watch the video I'm sending you.

524
54:45.470 --> 54:46.678
Breaking news.

525
54:46.762 --> 54:51.512
There is still an uproar outside this concert hall in Seoul.

526
54:51.595 --> 54:55.303
An 11-year-old girl who performed just hours before

527
54:55.387 --> 54:58.095
has been kidnapped by an unknown party.

528
54:58.178 --> 54:59.303
South Korea?

529
54:59.387 --> 55:03.470
The despicable crime was swiftly committed amid a crowd.

530
55:03.553 --> 55:07.512
-What's this? -A girl was kidnapped in Seoul.

531
55:07.595 --> 55:10.512
-At the same time as Saori. -So what?

532
55:10.595 --> 55:17.053
People in other Asian cities were kidnapped at the same time as Saori, too.

533
55:17.303 --> 55:19.095
Even the same rose petals.

534
55:21.887 --> 55:26.053
In Singapore, a man was abducted in a restaurant.

535
55:31.720 --> 55:35.762
-Ms. Janice? -Yeah. I've got this text from Tony.

536
55:37.595 --> 55:40.928
"Sorry, I’ll be a bit late...." "No hurry, take your time"

537
55:41.053 --> 55:45.178
-Is this the last time you communicate with him? -Yes.

538
55:52.095 --> 55:56.053
In Bangkok, a woman was taken from her home.

539
55:58.512 --> 56:00.345
You can't enter.

540
56:00.428 --> 56:02.387
I live here.

541
56:02.637 --> 56:03.678
Go on.

542
56:07.512 --> 56:10.220
Dao!! Come back!!

543
56:13.678 --> 56:17.803
In Manila, a young woman was abducted on her way home.

544
56:23.220 --> 56:24.428
Maria?!

545
56:26.137 --> 56:29.116
-Maria! -Sir! Do not enter, sir!

546
56:29.141 --> 56:31.641
Let me go! Maria’s my granddaughter!

547
56:31.705 --> 56:34.205
Please! Get back, sir. Please!

548
56:34.803 --> 56:39.012
In Taipei, a man was abducted in front of his daughter.

549
56:42.678 --> 56:43.553
Leona!

550
56:45.220 --> 56:47.678
Rui, come on.

551
56:49.137 --> 56:50.262
Mind your step.

552
56:52.053 --> 56:53.178
Leona.

553
56:58.085 --> 56:59.251
Dad...

554
57:05.512 --> 57:07.595
No photos!

555
57:13.345 --> 57:17.803
This isn't out yet, but there was a kidnapping in Naha, too.

556
57:20.762 --> 57:23.512
The perp may contact you. Wait here.

557
57:24.053 --> 57:25.012
Yes.

558
57:37.509 --> 57:41.443
Kidnappings occurred in seven Asian cities simultaneously.

559
57:41.659 --> 57:42.909
What's happening?

560
57:42.934 --> 57:45.142
I'll call when I know more.

561
57:50.053 --> 57:52.595
KIDNAPPINGS IN SEVEN ASIAN CITIES

562
57:52.678 --> 57:54.845
The world's in uproar about it!

563
57:57.720 --> 57:59.595
What on earth is going on?

564
58:00.383 --> 58:02.425
I'll check for updates.

565
58:07.470 --> 58:10.178
SAORI KIDNAP GAME

566
58:12.053 --> 58:14.053
"kiDnap GAME"?

567
58:17.790 --> 58:22.123
"You have been enlisted in the kiDnap GAME."

568
58:24.970 --> 58:26.484
"kiDnap GAME"?

569
58:28.055 --> 58:29.305
"Rules.

570
58:30.276 --> 58:32.526
"Each player has been given a mission."

571
58:34.856 --> 58:38.772
"Complete your mission before the others

572
58:39.100 --> 58:41.891
"if you want to save your loved one."

573
58:43.803 --> 58:46.678
"The time limit is ten days.

574
58:46.803 --> 58:52.887
"The game will end if a player completes the assigned mission."

575
58:55.053 --> 58:59.856
"Players deemed incapable of completing their mission will be

576
59:00.637 --> 59:03.137
"immediately disqualified."

577
59:03.303 --> 59:06.637
"Do not notify or request assistance from state authorities.

578
59:06.845 --> 59:10.178
"Rule-breakers will be disqualified.

579
59:10.553 --> 59:14.637
"Only one shall prevail... Only one shall survive..."

580
59:15.137 --> 59:18.012
Only one shall prevail...

581
59:20.720 --> 59:23.428
MISSION

582
59:42.845 --> 59:45.012
KIDNAP GAME CO-PRODUCTION PARTNERSHIP

583
59:45.095 --> 59:47.345
FUJI TELEVISION MAKERVILLE SIMSTORY

584
59:47.512 --> 59:51.387
BASED ON KIDNAP GAME CREATED BY YUSUKE KATO

585
59:51.387 --> 59:52.387
MkvDrama.net
